{"name":"Aggressive Baby Blue","hex":"#6fffff","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aggressive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Characterized by aggression; highly combative; prone to behave in a way that involves attacking (especially if unjustly) or arguing.","Tends to attack the player while unprovoked."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who is aggressive.","A (Black) woman who presents as masculine; a butch."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aggressive"},{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.\n\nA very young human, even if not yet born.","A very young human, even if not yet born."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baby blue","blocks":[{"text":"Baby blue, also called light blue, is a tint of azure, which is one of the pastel colors."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_blue"},{"title":"Aggression","blocks":[{"text":"Aggression is behavior aimed at opposing or attacking something or someone. Though often done with the intent to cause harm, some might channel it into creative and practical outlets. It may occur either reactively or without provocation. In humans, aggression can be caused by various triggers. For example, aggression may result from built-up frustration due to blocked goals or perceived disrespect. Human aggression can be classified into direct and indirect aggression; while the former is characterized by physical or verbal behavior intended to cause harm to someone, the latter is characterized by behavior intended to harm the social relations of an individual or group."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Agression_contre_Falli%C3%A8res_-_d%C3%A9tail_%28Petit_Parisien_illustr%C3%A9%2C_1909-01-10%29.jpeg/330px-Agression_contre_Falli%C3%A8res_-_d%C3%A9tail_%28Petit_Parisien_illustr%C3%A9%2C_1909-01-10%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aggression"},{"title":"Infant","blocks":[{"text":"An infant is a very young human being. Baby is an alternative term for infant. The terms may also be used to refer to juvenile beings of other organisms. A newborn is, in mainstream use, an infant who is only hours, days, or weeks old; while in medical contexts, a newborn or neonate is an infant in the first 28 days after birth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg/330px-The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infant"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Fynn_Esser_2013-11-18_21-47.jpg/500px-Fynn_Esser_2013-11-18_21-47.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Fynn_Esser_2013-11-18_21-47.jpg/500px-Fynn_Esser_2013-11-18_21-47.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Baby blue newborn male clothing","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFynn_Esser_2013-11-18_21-47.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg/500px-Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg/500px-Panthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Many mammals, such as the tiger, bare their teeth as a sign of aggression—a form of aposematism. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APanthera_tigris_altaica_28_-_Buffalo_Zoo_(1).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Elephant_seal_fight_Part-1.jpg/500px-Elephant_seal_fight_Part-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.